# SecPassGen Pro - Architecture

## System Overview
Next.js 14 app with NeonDB PostgreSQL. Generates cryptographically secure passwords with database-backed uniqueness verification.

## Core Components

### Frontend (`/app`, `/components`)
- **page.tsx**: Main UI with Lenis smooth scroll + Framer Motion
- **PasswordGenerator**: Password generation with API calls
- **PasswordHistory**: Encrypted local history (AES-256)
- **AnimatedBackground**: Visual effects

### Backend (`/app/api`)
- **POST /api/generate**: Password generation + uniqueness check
- **GET /api/stats**: Global statistics

### Database (`/lib/db.ts`)
- **generated_passwords**: Stores SHA-256 hashes
- **generation_stats**: Tracks total count
- Uses NeonDB serverless driver

### Security (`/lib/passwordHistory.ts`)
- Client-side AES-256 encryption
- Device-specific keys
- Auto-expires 24h
- Never sends to server

## Data Flow
1. User clicks generate
2. API generates password with crypto.getRandomValues()
3. SHA-256 hash checked against DB
4. If unique, stored + returned
5. Client encrypts + stores in localStorage
6. Stats updated via trigger

## Tech Stack
- Next.js 14 (App Router)
- TypeScript
- NeonDB (PostgreSQL)
- Tailwind + Radix UI
- Framer Motion + Lenis
- Web Crypto API

## Environment
```
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://...
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=https://passwords.sdad.pro
NEXT_PUBLIC_MAIN_DOMAIN=https://sdad.pro
```

## Deployment
Vercel (serverless) + NeonDB (pooled connection)
